# 0349 = 0348 + compiled-in steady-state defaults and cmdline slimming.
#   - 0348 retires 21 dead boot-arg parses (docs/202 tier A); 32 parses
#     remain including txsalv/txsoften/txreplay/rxskip.
#   - 0349 bakes the 15 steady-state knobs into compiled-in defaults
#     (rubyusb/usbirq/qmuirq/pad/dmauc/enum=3/winusb=4/ecmio/clr01/
#     rxbuf=2048/txgpd=2048/txreset/txsalv/txsoften/txbell); every
#     PE_parse stays so the cmdline can still override at runtime.
#   - The cmdline drops those tokens (596 -> 397 B of the 607 B budget),
#     leaving headroom for the upcoming ruby_txreplay round.
# Default path is unchanged for the device: same boots, same values, now
# sourced from the driver defaults instead of the boot line.
#
# Verified on the device (boot_a, 2026-11-21): banner values all sourced
# from the compiled-in defaults, 64 MB wget 14.1 MB/s + scp push
# 14.3 MB/s, TXRESET 0 for the whole session, salvage 2 + softbell 25 in
# the boot window (0347-level shape), rxpk ~93k rxerr=0, no panic.
# Not covered: EP2-5 host-side end-to-end, concurrency, suspend (0334
# boundaries unchanged); scp pull stays avoided (FIFOFULL half-fetch
# window, large files go through HTTP).
#
# patchset 1282a8bd486e22ef4acff0ee99e30c5babb0ba87bdd2cbe91f06b4ed9dae9b24
# (307 files: 82-file baseline with the 0010/0012 rewrites, 222 project
# patches through 0349, 3 historical; canonical composition of
# ci/prepare-baseline.sh — reproduces d87e666f... for the 0334 line exactly.
# Merge-window run 44918530808 green on this pin.)
# new in this pin: 0348 eff8fb2292834fb021e4a4260b89eb634243f84724cd6392b2bb9825da828752,
# 0349 0f3599c55b89c22112d400068ddb4937a972da948ccf2fe2a0aa94bd794b325f
# CI run 44912588343 (branch p3-usb-cl0349-defaults-slim-2026-11-21,
# format-gate green; patchset pin d87e666f... still the 0334 set, so the
# CI kernel there is NOT the 0349 kernel - the 0349 kernel is verified by
# the local VM build and on-device checks below).  Merge-window gate:
# dispatch run 44918530808 (green, full b1fa07fe...) and push run
# 44920381027 (green, full c03b36d7...) agree on exec-data 61c6b1a1...
# (same pin as the 0334 line - exec-data is insensitive to patch-comment
# and build-environment deltas, which is what makes it a usable gate).
KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA=61c6b1a138ff7c4a8014b9a643eb049dc19a23fdaec00ab093c555d2fa56472c
CI_KERNEL_SHA256=b1fa07fe1ba595e9e69c153d3b34b421d939daa3254c16989a3cac09a0e9f163
CI_KERNEL_EXEC_DATA_SHA256=61c6b1a138ff7c4a8014b9a643eb049dc19a23fdaec00ab093c555d2fa56472c
CI_IMAGE_SHA256=n/a (the CI workflow ships the kernel artifact; boot images are packed and hashed by the local pipeline)
BOOT_CMDLINE=config/0349-boot.cmdline
